            <ArticleTitle>Five-year prospective study of the effects of anxiety and depression in patients with coronary artery disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1135-8, A6, A9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Anxiety and depression have significant and widespread effects on daily function and symptoms of patients with coronary artery disease over a 5-year period. This may partially explain why results of treadmill stress testing and angiography poorly predict the daily functioning of patients with coronary artery disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
